---
// src/pages/surveys/wy-voter-access/info.astro
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../../../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../../../components/Footer.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Wyoming Voter Access - Skovgard 2026"
  description="Background on the Wyoming Voter Access Survey covering voting time, registration access, and election-day participation."
>
  <Nav />
  <main class="pt-20 bg-wy-bone min-h-screen">
    <section class="px-4 py-14 border-b border-black/10">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
        <p class="text-wy-sandstone font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-xs mb-3">Want to Know More?</p>
        <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-serif font-bold text-wy-charcoal mb-5">Wyoming Voter Access</h1>
        <p class="text-lg text-wy-charcoal/80 leading-relaxed">
          Voting should be simple, secure, and open to every eligible citizen.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="px-4 py-12">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6 text-wy-charcoal/90 leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          Wyoming already has a local election system run by county clerks, election workers,
          and community volunteers. The goal is to build on that system.
        </p>
        <p>
          This survey focuses on three simple ideas:
        </p>
        <ol class="space-y-4 list-decimal pl-5">
          <li>
            <strong>Give people time to vote.</strong>
            Create a statewide voting holiday for the primary and general election, or expand
            voting time access so working people have a fair chance to cast a ballot.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Make registration easier.</strong>
            Automatically register eligible Wyoming residents when getting or renewing a Wyoming
            driver&#8217;s license or state ID.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Protect same-day registration.</strong>
            Keep the ability for eligible citizens to register and vote on Election Day.
          </li>
        </ol>
        <p>
          The principle is simple: keep elections secure, verify eligibility, and make voting
          as easy as possible for every eligible Wyoming citizen.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="px-4 pb-12">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto bg-white border border-black/10 rounded-xl p-6 sm:p-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-serif font-bold text-wy-charcoal mb-4">Exact Survey Questions</h2>
        <ol class="space-y-5 list-decimal pl-5 text-wy-charcoal/90">
          <li>
            Should Wyoming create a statewide voting holiday for election days so eligible voters have time to vote?
            <ul class="mt-2 space-y-1 list-disc pl-5 text-sm text-wy-charcoal/80">
              <li>Yes, for both Primary Election Day and General Election Day</li>
              <li>Yes, for Primary Election Day only</li>
              <li>Yes, for General Election Day only</li>
              <li>Keep the current voting rules</li>
              <li>Not sure</li>
            </ul>
          </li>
          <li>
            Should eligible Wyoming residents be automatically registered to vote when getting or renewing a Wyoming driver&#8217;s license or state ID?
            <ul class="mt-2 space-y-1 list-disc pl-5 text-sm text-wy-charcoal/80">
              <li>Yes</li>
              <li>No</li>
              <li>Not sure</li>
            </ul>
          </li>
          <li>
            Should Wyoming protect same-day voter registration, so eligible citizens can register and vote on Election Day?
            <ul class="mt-2 space-y-1 list-disc pl-5 text-sm text-wy-charcoal/80">
              <li>Yes</li>
              <li>No</li>
              <li>Not sure</li>
            </ul>
          </li>
          <li>
            What would make voting access work better in Wyoming while keeping elections secure?
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-wy-charcoal/80">Optional long-text response.</p>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="px-4 pb-14">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2">
        <article class="bg-white border border-black/10 rounded-xl p-6">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-serif font-bold text-wy-charcoal mb-3">Fact Notes</h2>
          <ul class="space-y-3 text-sm text-wy-charcoal/85 leading-relaxed list-disc pl-5">
            <li>The 2026 Wyoming primary election is August 18, 2026.</li>
            <li>The 2026 Wyoming general election is November 3, 2026.</li>
            <li>Wyoming&#8217;s 2026 Secretary of State election calendar says voters may register and vote at polling places on Election Day.</li>
            <li>Wyoming law currently provides one hour of paid voting leave in certain circumstances under W.S. 22-2-111.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="bg-white border border-black/10 rounded-xl p-6">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-serif font-bold text-wy-charcoal mb-3">Source Notes</h2>
          <ul class="space-y-3 text-sm text-wy-charcoal/85 leading-relaxed list-disc pl-5">
            <li>
              Wyoming Secretary of State 2026 Key Election Dates:
              <a class="underline text-wy-ember hover:text-wy-ember-dark break-all"
                href="https://sos.wyo.gov/Elections/Docs/2026/2026_Key_Election_Dates.pdf"
                target="_blank" rel="noopener">sos.wyo.gov/Elections/Docs/2026/2026_Key_Election_Dates.pdf</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              Wyoming Statute 22-2-111, Employees time off to vote:
              <a class="underline text-wy-ember hover:text-wy-ember-dark break-all"
                href="https://wyoleg.gov/statutes/compress/title22.pdf"
                target="_blank" rel="noopener">wyoleg.gov/statutes/compress/title22.pdf</a>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>
